# reduced-explainer (M11): under reduced motion (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce; macOS's Reduce
# motion natively) the explainer only fades, 120 ms each way, where it rests (Callout.module.css: no
# --callout-from). a's chip rested on: the opening's frames at 0, 40, 80 and 120 ms; then the
# pointer onto the top bar: the closing's frames at 0, 48, 96 and gone. Inputs and closing shots
# fall on the 16 ms grid: a closing explainer is gone at its exit's end, React's at that instant,
# the port's from its next frame.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
reduced-motion on
wait 2000
move 70 424
wait 400
shot open-0000
wait 40
shot open-0040
wait 40
shot open-0080
wait 40
shot open-0120
wait 504
move 760 48
shot leave-0000
wait 48
shot leave-0048
wait 48
shot leave-0096
wait 32
shot leave-gone
